     Update from V1.04 -> V1.04B

     This is not a scheduled update, but more a bug fix so don't
     expect big suprises.
     At some systems V1.04 looked a bit unstable, but this seems
     to be solved with a recompile of the BBS executable.



     If my BBS number (+31-599-564696) can't be reached anymore in
     the next few weeks it is because of changes to the phonelines here.

     A number of lines of the business in the house here are changed
     to ISDN lines. (My BBS line is part of the business)
     I don't know yet what the new number will be but I will be Unit 7
     on one of the lines.
     There should be a tape on the old lines with a recording of the
     new number. It isn't 100% sure that the number is changed
     because the fellow I spoke later told me the number would
     be the same .. but that person also told me that we should be
     callable with every modem. Which is a but strange.
     The point is that the PTT is convincing people to convert
     to ISDN by calling them often and sending them folders with
     personal deals with things that would else be options
     that cost money like conversions kits with A/B converters.

     Note that on the new line you won't get a connect higher
     then 14400 baud because I don't actually have a budget
     for a new modem.

     But in the business (not mine) there will be a Pentium 200Mhz
     with an internal U.S. Robotics (now 3com) V34/ISDN .. so if you get
     a ISDN connect (64000 baud) you know something went wrong with ISDN
     and you are on the wrong machine.

     If you loose all contact to me because something goes
